WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.325
Level three: Software Design.

2
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:07.212
Process Modelling gave us Commands and Events — but what enforces the rules?

3
00:00:07.212 --> 00:00:13.350
The Aggregate emerges — a consistency boundary that decides and emits the event.

4
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.387
A Command acts on an Aggregate, or an external system, to produce that event.

5
00:00:18.387 --> 00:00:24.550
So Software Design is Process Modelling plus the Aggregate — almost a spec for code.

6
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.362
Some behaviour spans several Aggregates.

7
00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:31.237
A Process Manager coordinates them — a stateful saga.

8
00:00:31.237 --> 00:00:35.012
It starts on one Aggregate's event, then commands the next.

9
00:00:35.012 --> 00:00:40.512
That events back, so it sends the next command — advancing its state with each round.

10
00:00:40.512 --> 00:00:47.337
…until the process is final: one long-running transaction, kept consistent across aggregates.

11
00:00:47.337 --> 00:00:52.712
Aggregates with behaviour, synced by Process Managers — the blueprint for code.

